Deduplicated":11}},{"Use":[{"Move":{"kind":{"Local":148},"ty":{"Deduplicated":11}}},"Yes"]}]},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":232},"kind":{"StorageDead":147},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":303},"kind":{"StorageDead":143},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":303},"kind":{"StorageDead":141},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"Deduplicated":303},"kind":{"StorageDead":139},"comments_before":[]}],"terminator":{"span":{"Deduplicated":227},"kind":{"Goto":{"target":87}},"comments_before":[]},"is_cleanup":false}],"comments":[[51,["The basic algorithm is, for every byte:","  a = (a + byte) % MOD","  b = (b + a) % MOD","where MOD = 65521.","","For efficiency, we can defer the `% MOD` operations as long as neither a nor b overflows:","- Between calls to `write`, we ensure that a and b are always in range 0..MOD.","- We use 32-bit arithmetic in this function.","- Therefore, a and b must not increase by more than 2^32-MOD without performing a `% MOD`","  operation.","","According to Wikipedia, b is calculated as follows for non-incremental checksumming:","  b = n×D1 + (n−1)×D2 + (n−2)×D3 + ... + Dn + n*1 (mod 65521)","Where n is the number of bytes and Di is the i-th Byte. We need to change this to account","for the previous values of a and b, as well as treat every input Byte as being 255:","  b_inc = n×255 + (n-1)×255 + ... + 255 + n*65520","Or in other words:","  b_inc = n*65520 + n(n+1)/2*255","The max chunk size is thus the largest value of n so that b_inc <= 2^32-65521.","  2^32-65521 = n*65520 + n(n+1)/2*255","Plugging this into an equation solver since I can't math gives n = 5552.18..., so 5552.","","On top of the optimization outlined above, the algorithm can also be parallelized with a","bit more work:","","Note that b is a linear combination of a vector of input bytes (D1, ..., Dn).","","If we fix some value k<N and rewrite indices 1, ..., N as","","  1_1, 1_2, ..., 1_k, 2_1, ..., 2_k, ..., (N/k)_k,","","then we can express a and b in terms of sums of smaller sequences kb and ka:","","  ka(j) := D1_j + D2_j + ... + D(N/k)_j where j <= k","  kb(j) := (N/k)*D1_j + (N/k-1)*D2_j + ... + D(N/k)_j where j <= k",""," a = ka(1) + ka(2) + ... + ka(k) + 1"," b = k*(kb(1) + kb(2) + ... + kb(k)) - 1*ka(2) - ...  - (k-1)*ka(k) + N","","We use this insight to unroll the main loop and process k=4 bytes at a time.","The resulting code is highly amenable to SIMD acceleration, although the immediate speedups","stem from increased pipeline parallelism rather than auto-vectorization.","","This technique is described in-depth (here:)[https://software.intel.com/content/www/us/\\","en/develop/articles/fast-computation-of-fletcher-checksums.html]"]],[63,["iterate over 4 bytes at a time"]],[78,["special-case the final chunk because it may be shorter than the rest"]],[89,["combine the sub-sum results into the main sum"]],[101,["iterate over the remaining few bytes in serial"]]]}}},{"def_id":7,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["convert",0]},{"Ident":["num",0]},{"Impl":{"Trait":1}},{"Ident":["from",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":6,"beg":{"line":151,"col":12},"end":{"line":151,"col":42}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":"Converts from [`u16`] to [`u32`] losslessly."}],"inline":"Always","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Opaque","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":9}],"output":{"Deduplicated":11}},"src":{"TraitImpl":{"impl_ref":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}},"trait_ref":{"id":6,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11},{"Deduplicated":9}],"const_generics":[],"trait_r